{"name":"Wine Red","hex":"#7b0323","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An alcoholic beverage made by fermenting grape juice, with an ABV ranging from 5.5–16%.","An alcoholic beverage made by fermenting other substances, producing a similar ABV."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To entertain (someone) with wine.","To drink wine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wine"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wine red","blocks":[{"text":"The color wine, or wine red, also called bordeaux, vinous, or vinaceous, is a dark shade of red and brown. It is a representation of the typical color of red wine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c0/Red_Wine_Glass.jpg/330px-Red_Wine_Glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine_red"},{"title":"Wine","blocks":[{"text":"Wine is an alcoholic drink made from fermented grape juice. It is produced and consumed in many regions around the world, in a wide variety of styles which are influenced by different varieties of grapes, growing environments, viticulture methods, and production techniques."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Red_and_white_wine_in_glass.jpg/330px-Red_and_white_wine_in_glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine"},{"titl